{"title":"The Beautiful Rouge National Urban Park","startsAt":"2026-10-10T08:30:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-10T10:30:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"This classic Rouge Valley hike features excellent examples of rare Carolinian ecosystems while traversing a 200-year-old former logging route where pine trees were cut and floated down the river, eventually bound for ship building yards in Europe.\nThis is an intermediate hike.\nWe will be parking at Rouge National Urban Park, Twyn Rivers Day Use Area. 55 Twyn Rivers Dr, Scarborough, ON M1B 5R9\nIf you get lost, please call my cell: 647-949-6912\n\n**Important Reminder:**\nBy participating in this hike, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to the Liability Waiver and Acknowledgement of Risk. If you have not done so, we kindly request that you refrain from participating in this event. We appreciate your cooperation and look forward to an enjoyable and safe adventure!\n• Arrive on time! Please be punctual, as the group will leave on time.\n• Know your limits! Choose the hike that match your fitness level.","venue":{"name":"Twyn Rivers Parking Lot","address":"55 Twyn Rivers Drive, Toronto","lat":43.814354,"lng":-79.15399,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Forest Footprints","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/0/9/d/highres_525436541.jpeg"}